    "q-106003": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106003",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What are the coordinates of the minimum point of the function $y=(x+2)^{2}+5?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the graph of $y=(x-h)^{2}+k$ is a translation of the standard parabola $y={x}^{2}$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up.\n\nThe vertex of $y=(x-h)^{2}+k$ is located at $(h,k).$\n\nHere, the parabola is translated $2$ units *left*, so we have $h=-2.$ The parabola is also translated $5$ units *up*, so we have $k=5.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218419/assets/8e69ca48e852176d2ed258f062995835889374975492873fe0863ea782d87ebd.png)\n\nThe vertex is located at $(-2,5),$ and these are the coordinates of the minimum point.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
